{"1-1":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G2471","lemma":"ἰσότης","tr":"isotēs","gloss":"equality","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G2962","lemma":"κύριος","tr":"kurios","gloss":"lord: God","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":714},{"base":"G3930","lemma":"παρέχω","tr":"parechō","gloss":"to furnish occasion","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"G1342","lemma":"δίκαιος","tr":"dikaios","gloss":"just","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":79},{"base":"G1401","lemma":"δοῦλος","tr":"doulos","gloss":"slave","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":129},{"base":"G3772","lemma":"οὐρανός","tr":"ouranos","gloss":"heaven","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":272},{"base":"G6063","lemma":"οἶδα","tr":"oida","gloss":"to know","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":283},{"base":"G2192","lemma":"ἔχω","tr":"echō","gloss":"to have","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":707}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"because you know that the Lord will reward each one for whatever good he does, whether he is slave or free.","from":1},{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"for which I am an ambassador in chains. Pray that I may proclaim it fearlessly, as I should.","from":1},{"book":"JAS","chapter":2,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"For judgment without mercy will be shown to anyone who has not been merciful. Mercy triumphs over judgment.","from":1},{"book":"REV","chapter":17,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"They will make war against the Lamb, and the Lamb will triumph over them, because He is Lord of lords and King of kings; and He will be accompanied by His called and chosen and faithful ones.”","from":1},{"book":"DEU","chapter":24,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"Do not oppress a hired hand who is poor and needy, whether he is a brother or a foreigner residing in one of your towns.","from":1},{"book":"DEU","chapter":24,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"You are to pay his wages each day before sunset, because he is poor and depends on them. Otherwise he may cry out to the LORD against you, and you will be guilty of sin.","from":1},{"book":"LUK","chapter":16,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"Jesus also said to His disciples, “There was a rich man whose manager was accused of wasting his possessions.","from":1},{"book":"LUK","chapter":16,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"No servant can serve two masters. Either he will hate the one and love the other, or he will be devoted to the one and despise the other. You cannot serve both God and money.”","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"2-6":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":3}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G1163","lemma":"δεῖ","tr":"dei","gloss":"be necessary","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":101},{"base":"G2980","lemma":"λαλέω","tr":"laleō","gloss":"to speak","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":294},{"base":"G3056","lemma":"λόγος","tr":"logos","gloss":"word","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":329},{"base":"G0741","lemma":"ἀρτύω","tr":"artuō","gloss":"to season","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G1805","lemma":"ἐξαγοράζω","tr":"exagorazō","gloss":"to redeem","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G2443","lemma":"ἵνα","tr":"hina","gloss":"in order that","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":668},{"base":"G0217","lemma":"ἅλας","tr":"halas","gloss":"salt","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"G0260","lemma":"ἅμα","tr":"hama","gloss":"together","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"G4342","lemma":"προσκαρτερέω","tr":"proskartereō","gloss":"to continue in","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"G2169","lemma":"εὐχαριστία","tr":"eucharistia","gloss":"thankfulness","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":15}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1TH","chapter":5,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":73,"source":"openbible","text":"Pray without ceasing.","from":2},{"book":"1TH","chapter":5,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":73,"source":"openbible","text":"Give thanks in every circumstance, for this is Godʼs will for you in Christ Jesus.","from":2},{"book":"EPH","chapter":4,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":71,"source":"both","text":"Let no unwholesome talk come out of your mouths, but only what is helpful for building up the one in need and bringing grace to those who listen.","from":6},{"book":"1PE","chapter":3,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":51,"source":"openbible","text":"But in your hearts sanctify Christ as Lord. Always be prepared to give a defense to everyone who asks you the reason for the hope that is in you. But respond with gentleness and respect,","from":6},{"book":"PHP","chapter":4,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":46,"source":"both","text":"Be anxious for nothing, but in everything, by prayer and petition, with thanksgiving, present your requests to God.","from":2},{"book":"ECC","chapter":10,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":40,"source":"both","text":"The words of a wise manʼs mouth are gracious, but the lips of a fool consume him.","from":6},{"book":"EPH","chapter":5,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":40,"source":"openbible","text":"Pay careful attention, then, to how you walk, not as unwise but as wise,","from":5},{"book":"EPH","chapter":5,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":40,"source":"openbible","text":"Therefore do not be foolish, but understand what the Lordʼs will is.","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"7-9":{"people":[{"id":"tychicus-g5190","name":"Tychicus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"onesimus-g3682","name":"Onesimus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G1107","lemma":"γνωρίζω","tr":"gnōrizō","gloss":"to make known","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":25},{"base":"G0027","lemma":"ἀγαπητός","tr":"agapētos","gloss":"beloved","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":61},{"base":"G4103","lemma":"πιστός","tr":"pistos","gloss":"faithful","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":67},{"base":"G0080","lemma":"ἀδελφός","tr":"adelphos","gloss":"brother","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":343},{"base":"G3682","lemma":"Ὀνήσιμος","tr":"Onēsimos","gloss":"Onesimus","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G5190","lemma":"Τυχικός","tr":"Tuchikos","gloss":"Tychicus","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"G4889","lemma":"σύνδουλος","tr":"sundoulos","gloss":"fellow slave","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"G1249","lemma":"διάκονος","tr":"diakonos","gloss":"servant","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":29},{"base":"G5602","lemma":"ὧδε","tr":"hōde","gloss":"here","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":61},{"base":"G3992","lemma":"πέμπω","tr":"pempō","gloss":"to send","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":79}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PHM","chapter":1,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"I appeal to you for my child Onesimus, whose father I became while I was in chains.","from":9},{"book":"PHM","chapter":1,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"I, Paul, write this with my own hand. I will repay it—not to mention that you owe me your very self.","from":9},{"book":"ACT","chapter":20,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Paul was accompanied by Sopater son of Pyrrhus from Berea, Aristarchus and Secundus from Thessalonica, Gaius from Derbe, Timothy, and Tychicus and Trophimus from the province of Asia.","from":7},{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Tychicus, the beloved brother and faithful servant in the Lord, will tell you everything, so that you also may know about me and what I am doing.","from":7},{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Peace to the brothers and love with faith from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.","from":7},{"book":"2TI","chapter":4,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Tychicus, however, I have sent to Ephesus.","from":7},{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"I have sent him to you for this very purpose, that you may know about us, and that he may encourage your hearts.","from":8},{"book":"ISA","chapter":40,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“Comfort, comfort My people,” says your God.","from":8}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2}]},"10-14":{"people":[{"id":"aristarchus-g0708","name":"Aristarchus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"barnabas-g0921g","name":"Barnabas","kind":"person","brief":"Brother of Mary","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"father-of-barnabas-g0921h","name":"father of Barnabas","kind":"person","brief":"From Levi","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"mark-g3138","name":"Mark","kind":"person","brief":"Paul's companian","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"justus-g2459h","name":"Justus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"epaphras-g1889","name":"Epaphras","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"demas-g1214","name":"Demas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"luke-g3065","name":"Luke","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"places":[{"id":"hierapolis-g2404","name":"Hierapolis","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"laodicea-g2993","name":"Laodicea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"words":[{"base":"G0782","lemma":"ἀσπάζομαι","tr":"aspazomai","gloss":"to pay respects to","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":60},{"base":"G5228","lemma":"ὑπέρ","tr":"huper","gloss":"above","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":156},{"base":"G1214","lemma":"Δημᾶς","tr":"Dēmas","gloss":"Demas","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G1889","lemma":"Ἐπαφρᾶς","tr":"Epaphras","gloss":"Epaphras","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G2459","lemma":"Ἰοῦστος","tr":"Ioustos","gloss":"Justus","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G3065","lemma":"Λουκᾶς","tr":"Loukas","gloss":"Luke","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G4869","lemma":"συναιχμάλωτος","tr":"sunaichmalōtos","gloss":"fellow prisoner","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G4192","lemma":"πόνος","tr":"ponos","gloss":"travail","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G0708","lemma":"Ἀρίσταρχος","tr":"Aristarchos","gloss":"Aristarchus","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"G2993","lemma":"Λαοδίκεια","tr":"Laodikeia","gloss":"Laodicea","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ROM","chapter":15,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Now I urge you, brothers, by our Lord Jesus Christ and by the love of the Spirit, to join me in my struggle by praying to God for me.","from":12},{"book":"PHM","chapter":1,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"as do Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers.","from":14},{"book":"ACT","chapter":11,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"So when Peter went up to Jerusalem, the circumcised believers took issue with him","from":11},{"book":"COL","chapter":1,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"For this reason, since the day we heard about you, we have not stopped praying for you and asking God to fill you with the knowledge of His will in all spiritual wisdom and understanding,","from":12},{"book":"COL","chapter":1,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"You learned it from Epaphras, our beloved fellow servant, who is a faithful minister of Christ on our behalf,","from":12},{"book":"COL","chapter":1,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"We proclaim Him, admonishing and teaching everyone with all wisdom, so that we may present everyone perfect in Christ.","from":12},{"book":"PHM","chapter":1,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ Jesus, sends you greetings,","from":12},{"book":"ACT","chapter":10,"verse":45,"verseEnd":45,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"All the circumcised believers who had accompanied Peter were astounded that the gift of the Holy Spirit had been poured out even on the Gentiles.","from":11}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":7},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":4},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":3},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":3}]},"15-18":{"people":[{"id":"nympha-g3564","name":"Nympha","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"archippus-g0751","name":"Archippus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"onesimus-g3682","name":"Onesimus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"tychicus-g5190","name":"Tychicus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18}],"places":[{"id":"laodicea-g2993","name":"Laodicea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"colossae-g2857g","name":"Colossae","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"rome-g4514","name":"Rome","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18}],"words":[{"base":"G0314","lemma":"ἀναγινώσκω","tr":"anaginōskō","gloss":"to read","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":32},{"base":"G2993","lemma":"Λαοδίκεια","tr":"Laodikeia","gloss":"Laodicea","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"G2443","lemma":"ἵνα","tr":"hina","gloss":"in order that","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":668},{"base":"G1577","lemma":"ἐκκλησία","tr":"ekklēsia","gloss":"assembly","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":114},{"base":"G0751","lemma":"Ἄρχιππος","tr":"Archippos","gloss":"Archippus","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G0783","lemma":"ἀσπασμός","tr":"aspasmos","gloss":"salutation","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"G1199","lemma":"δεσμός","tr":"desmos","gloss":"chain","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"G3421","lemma":"μνημονεύω","tr":"mnēmoneuō","gloss":"to remember","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":21},{"base":"G1992","lemma":"ἐπιστολή","tr":"epistolē","gloss":"epistle","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"G1248","lemma":"διακονία","tr":"diakonia","gloss":"service","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":34}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1TH","chapter":5,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"I charge you before the Lord to have this letter read to all the brothers.","from":16},{"book":"PHM","chapter":1,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"to Apphia our sister, to Archippus our fellow soldier, and to the church that meets at your house:","from":17},{"book":"ACT","chapter":1,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"He was one of our number and shared in this ministry.”","from":17},{"book":"HEB","chapter":13,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Remember those in prison as if you were bound with them, and those who are mistreated as if you were suffering with them.","from":18},{"book":"EZK","chapter":44,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"They are to teach My people the difference between the holy and the common, and show them how to discern between the clean and the unclean.","from":17},{"book":"EZK","chapter":44,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"In any dispute, they shall officiate as judges and judge according to My ordinances. They must keep My laws and statutes regarding all My appointed feasts, and they must keep My Sabbaths holy.","from":17},{"book":"ROM","chapter":16,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Greet also the church that meets at their house. Greet my beloved Epenetus, who was the first convert to Christ in the province of Asia.","from":15},{"book":"1CO","chapter":16,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"This greeting is in my own hand—Paul.","from":18}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":3}]}}